Tencent DSpine inference algorithm
----------------------------------
The Metal selection, chain and feature bridge kernels under
crates/lisa-metal/src/shaders/dspine/ adapt the algorithms in
sglang_dspine/kernels/dspine.py at the revision below. Selection preserves
Lisa's stable total order and the bridge retains MLX's composed arithmetic.
normalize.metal and normalize_codes.metal preserve Apple's MLX 0.32.4
row_reduce_simple reduction design (Copyright 2023-2024 Apple Inc., MIT;
full license above), including read order and simd_sum stages.

The optional Qwen 3.8 27B DSpine drafter in
crates/lisa-models/src/qwen3_5/dspine/ and its weight bindings in
crates/lisa-engine/src/bindings/dspine.rs follow the inference design
in https://github.com/Tencent/DSpine at revision
321b0fc1388c4cdf03483ab73856975f7c0c0be7. The upstream project is licensed
under Apache-2.0; this implementation is an independent Rust/Metal port.
Checkpoint weights are distributed under their own model license.
Vocabulary projection tables follow dspine_mlx/dspine_mlx/bridge.py at that
revision with shape-matched native matmuls. dspine_retrieval.rs implements a
native affine 2-bit counterpart to the upstream coarse-head/top-128-rescore
design; it does not import CUDA FP8 arithmetic or weights.
The measured SPS policy in dspine_policy.rs and compact-history Metal GDN
verification/commit design also follow that revision's
sglang_dspine/verification/policy.py and runtime/replayssm/. The Metal kernels
retain Lisa's sequential GDN arithmetic; they do not copy CUDA matrix math.

